# Free models a default `dispatch.sh opencode` task (and every clawock-patrol round) tries, in
# order. The first line is the primary; the rest are the fallback pool the runner rotates through
# (after the last one it wraps back to the first). The pool is read at dispatch time, so edits
# apply without restarting the patrol service.
#
# Every entry must be in the Zen catalog (`opencode models opencode`) and cost nothing. The runner
# allows 2 attempts per pool line, so a dead entry is two wasted attempts per failing round.
#
# 2026-10-08 reorder, from the patrol run logs of 10-07..10-08 (307 attempts in 45 rounds) and a
# tool probe of the whole catalog at 20:41. What decides the order is still how a model behaves
# while the free tier throttles it (HTTP 429 FreeUsageLimitError, "Rate limit exceeded"): the
# limit is per model, and a model that hides it costs the runner's full 300s stall timer.
#   * longcat-2.5-preview-free and nemotron-3-ultra-free stay first. They finish the morning
#     rounds (10-08 08:47-14:00, attempt 1 or 2) and mostly surface the 429 afterwards, so a
#     throttled try ends in about 80s (longcat 49 of 49 failures, nemotron 19 of 33 with 11 stalls).
#   * fledge-alpha-free (1M context) moves from 8th to 3rd. It finished all 9 rounds of
#     10-07 21:08-10-08 00:55 and 10-08 16:10-20:20, each time as attempt 8, after about 25 minutes
#     spent on the seven lines ahead of it. Those rounds read as "ok" in rounds.tsv.
#   * ling-3.1-flash-free moves from 9th to 4th: probe OK, and its only daytime-quality run
#     worked for 40 minutes before a 503. It was reached 6 times, all inside a dead window.
#   * space-bunny-free and mimo-v2.6-flash-free retry the 429 silently (74 stalls, 6 finished
#     rounds in two days), so they sit behind every model that fails fast or works.
#   * removed: muse-spark-1.3-contributor-free (0 of 43 attempts since 10-06, 39 stalls) and
#     ling-3.0-flash-fin-free (0 of 29, all stalls). Each cost 300s per failing pass. exo-free
#     answers "Endpoint is unavailable" (15 of 15) but fails in 90s, so it stays as the last
#     line, where it is free to return. Earlier removals: mimo-v2.5-free, union-alpha.
#   * left out on purpose: big-pickle (2025 stealth, 200k context) and nemotron-3.5-lightning-free
#     (small fast tier) - kcn wants good models first. opencode-go is not an option: the key in
#     ~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json has no active subscription.
#
# Some windows have no working model at all (10-07 00:50-07:57 and 16:48-19:56, 10-08
# 01:06-07:57: 0 finished attempts out of 163); no order helps there, and the patrol supervisor
# backs off by itself. Both nights ended at 07:57 (23:57 UTC), which points at a daily reset.
# This order went stale within a day once already. Re-probe before trusting it:
#   /root/tools/agent-dispatch/probe-free-models.sh --tool $(sed 's/#.*//' <this file>)
opencode/longcat-2.5-preview-free
opencode/nemotron-3-ultra-free
opencode/fledge-alpha-free
opencode/ling-3.1-flash-free
opencode/space-bunny-free
opencode/mimo-v2.6-flash-free
opencode/exo-free
